 "equipment_type": "Packaged ventilation unit / make-up air controller (DOAS, energy recovery)",
 "applies_to": "Modine Atherion MPR commercial packaged ventilation units and ERM energy recovery modules running Modine Control System program series 3 and 4.",
 "summary": "The Modine Control System is a Carel pCO3 controller in MPR packaged ventilation units, optionally with an ERM energy recovery module. A plug-in card gives BACnet IP/Ethernet or BACnet MS/TP (LonWorks and Modbus are other options). The BMS can switch the unit on and off, send an occupied command, reset alarms and write supply-air, neutral-air, dewpoint, humidity and CO2 setpoints. Readings cover temperatures, humidity, CO2, refrigerant circuit values, demands, damper and fan modulation, switch inputs, relay outputs and alarms.",
 "bacnet_transport": [
  "BACnet IP",
  "BACnet MS/TP"
 ],
 "firmware": "Modine Control System program version series 3 and 4",
 "default_device_instance": null,
 "access_inferred": false,
 "notes": [
  "Object names here are the Carel variable names printed in the manual; the BACnet column gives only the object address (AVn / BVn). Check the names your BACnet card reports.",
  "Carel analog variables are AV 1-39, Carel integer variables are AV 1001-1084 and digital variables are BV 1-69.",
  "The manual titles the table 'Typical BMS / EMS / BAS System Variables'; ERM, compressor, gas and electric heat points only carry data when those options are fitted.",
  "Engineering units are not printed in the table.",
  "The manual swaps the LonWorks variables on BV 4 (smoke) and BV 5 (filter); the BACnet descriptions are shown as printed.",
  "Source table: manual pages 87-94 (138 objects)."
 ],
